# =====================================================================
# Paragon Chat - example Tor configuration (HiddenService)
# =====================================================================
#
# This is an EXAMPLE. Do NOT copy this file over your real torrc verbatim.
# Merge the lines you need into the torrc of your Tor instance.
#
# On Windows, torrc is usually:
#   C:\Users\<you>\Desktop\Tor Browser\Browser\TorBrowser\Data\Tor\torrc
# or for a standalone tor install:
#   C:\Program Files\Tor\torrc
#
# After editing, RESTART Tor so it loads the HiddenService keys.
# =====================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) SOCKS port
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paragon connects OUT to remote .onion peers through this SOCKS5 proxy.
# Default 9050 matches a standalone Tor daemon.
# Tor Browser uses 9150 instead; if so, also set PARAGON_SOCKS_PORT=9150
# before launching Paragon.
SocksPort 9050

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) HiddenService (your own .onion address)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# HiddenServiceDir  = the folder Paragon wrote on "Generate onion identity".
#                     It contains hostname, hs_ed25519_public_key,
#                     hs_ed25519_secret_key. Do NOT commit this folder.
# HiddenServicePort = <VIRTUAL_PORT> <TARGET_HOST>:<TARGET_PORT>
#                     VIRTUAL_PORT = the port advertised on your .onion
#                                    (must match the "Port" in Paragon ID)
#                     TARGET       = where Paragon actually listens locally
#                                    (127.0.0.1 + listen port; default 9001)
#
# Example: identity generated with Port = 9001, HS dir = .\hs_9001
#
HiddenServiceDir C:\Paragon\hs_9001
HiddenServicePort 9001 127.0.0.1:9001

# If Paragon listens on a different local port (PARAGON_LISTEN_PORT), use:
#   HiddenServicePort 9001 127.0.0.1:9010

# If you run MULTIPLE identities, add one HiddenService block per identity:
#   HiddenServiceDir C:\Paragon\hs_9001
#   HiddenServicePort 9001 127.0.0.1:9001
#
#   HiddenServiceDir C:\Paragon\hs_9002
#   HiddenServicePort 9002 127.0.0.1:9002


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Optional: onion v3 only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paragon only ever talks to .onion when onion_only=True, so this is
# informational. v3 onions are required for modern Tor anyway.
# HiddenServiceVersion 3


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4) Optional: faster descriptor publish (default is fine)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing your onion descriptor normally takes 30-60 seconds after
# Tor restart. Leave defaults unless you know what you are doing.
#
# PublishHidServDescriptors 1
